      <aside class="article__aside">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          This thesis develops a mathematically rigorous account of the relationship between
          calculus and the perception of musical consonance and dissonance. It treats equal
          temperament, sinusoidal pressure, harmonic structure, and Fourier decomposition as
          the main analytic tools.
        </p>
      </aside>
